# XSH setresuid
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
# setresuid() is only called in child processes. Values 60001-60003 are used
# only by privileged children; no EINVAL test (no value is portably invalid).

assertion  XSH.setresuid.001
anchor     functions/setresuid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/setresuid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       setresuid(-1, -1, -1) returns 0 and none of the three IDs changes.
test       t/001-minus-one.c

assertion  XSH.setresuid.002
anchor     functions/setresuid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       A child calls setresuid() with its current saved, real and effective IDs
           in that order (each is a value it already holds); it returns 0 and
           getresuid() then reports real = old saved, effective = old real, saved =
           old effective.
test       t/002-own-values.c

assertion  XSH.setresuid.003
anchor     functions/setresuid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       A privileged child calls setresuid() with three different values (60001,
           60002, 60003); it returns 0 and getresuid() reports exactly those.
needs      root
test       t/003-any-values.c

assertion  XSH.setresuid.004
anchor     functions/setresuid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       After that, setresuid(-1, 60001, -1) returns 0 and changes only the
           effective ID, setresuid(60003, -1, -1) changes only the real ID.
needs      root
test       t/004-minus-one-keeps.c

assertion  XSH.setresuid.005
anchor     functions/setresuid.html#ERRORS/EPERM
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       A child without privileges calling setresuid() with a value it does not
           hold, as the real, as the effective or as the saved ID (one call each),
           fails with EPERM and none of the IDs changes.
note       When the suite runs as root the child gives up privilege with
           setuid/setgid first (all three IDs).
test       t/005-eperm.c
